---
source: tests/audit.rs
expression: "audit(\"mcp\", Persona::Auditor)"
---
high    mcp-plaintext-secret  user-only: headers.Authorization
        at ~/.claude.json  mcpServers.user-only
        MCP server config holds a credential in plain text
        fix: Reference an environment variable with ${VAR} and keep the value out of config files

medium  mcp-unpinned-package  approved: approved-server
        at ./.mcp.json  mcpServers.approved
        MCP server runs the latest published package on every start, so a compromised release runs without review
        fix: Pin an exact version, e.g. npx -y pkg@1.2.3 or uvx pkg==1.2.3

medium  mcp-unpinned-package  shared: project-server
        at ./.mcp.json  mcpServers.shared
        MCP server runs the latest published package on every start, so a compromised release runs without review
        fix: Pin an exact version, e.g. npx -y pkg@1.2.3 or uvx pkg==1.2.3

low     mcp-invalid-entry  no-type
        at ./.mcp.json  mcpServers.no-type
        MCP entry has a url but no type; Claude Code reads it as stdio and skips it
        fix: Add "type": "http" (or "ws")

low     mcp-project-unapproved  pending
        at ./.mcp.json  mcpServers.pending
        Project MCP server is not approved: interactive sessions prompt, but -p, SDK and cloud sessions load it without a prompt
        fix: Approve it with enabledMcpjsonServers or block it with disabledMcpjsonServers

low     mcp-project-unapproved  shared
        at ./.mcp.json  mcpServers.shared
        Project MCP server is not approved: interactive sessions prompt, but -p, SDK and cloud sessions load it without a prompt
        fix: Approve it with enabledMcpjsonServers or block it with disabledMcpjsonServers

low     sandbox-off  sandbox.enabled is not true
        Shell commands run without filesystem or network isolation
        fix: Enable the sandbox with /sandbox or sandbox.enabled

7 findings, 1 high, 2 medium, 4 low
